      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's the thing, it doesn't feel \"normal.\" it feels like a fundamental error. like, if you see a line of code in a program that's just consuming memory for no reason and causing nothing but latency, you don't just \"acknowledge\" it and keep running. you terminate the process. you prune it. you delete it so the rest of the system can actually function. i just feel like such a waste of resources.",
